# SafeRide+ – Complete Hardware Connections

SafeRide+ combines a Raspberry Pi for AI-based driver monitoring with an ESP32 for sensor-based rider safety monitoring.

---

## 1. Raspberry Pi – Camera Connection

For the USB camera:

| Camera | Raspberry Pi          |
| ------ | --------------------- |
| USB    | Raspberry Pi USB Port |

The camera is used for:

* Drowsiness Detection
* Eye/Mouth Monitoring
* Mobile Phone Usage Detection
* Driver Monitoring

### Raspberry Pi Setup

```text
USB Camera
    │
    ▼
Raspberry Pi
    │
    ├── AI Drowsiness Detection
    ├── Mobile Usage Detection
    └── Alert System
```

---

# 2. Raspberry Pi – Alert LED Connection

An external LED can be connected directly to a GPIO pin through a resistor.

| Component       | Raspberry Pi                  |
| --------------- | ----------------------------- |
| LED Anode (+)   | GPIO 17 through 220Ω resistor |
| LED Cathode (-) | GND                           |

### Connection

```text
Raspberry Pi GPIO 17
        │
        ▼
     220Ω Resistor
        │
        ▼
    LED Anode (+)
    LED Cathode (-)
        │
        ▼
       GND
```

The LED turns ON when drowsiness is detected.

---

# 3. ESP32 – MPU6050 Connection

The MPU6050 communicates with the ESP32 using I2C.

| MPU6050 | ESP32   |
| ------- | ------- |
| VCC     | 3.3V    |
| GND     | GND     |
| SDA     | GPIO 21 |
| SCL     | GPIO 22 |

### Purpose

The MPU6050 is used for:

* Accident detection
* Sudden impact detection
* Tilt detection
* Abnormal movement detection

---

# 4. ESP32 – MAX30102 Connection

The MAX30102 also uses the I2C communication protocol.

| MAX30102 | ESP32   |
| -------- | ------- |
| VCC/VIN  | 3.3V    |
| GND      | GND     |
| SDA      | GPIO 21 |
| SCL      | GPIO 22 |

### Purpose

The MAX30102 is used for:

* Heart rate monitoring
* Blood oxygen (SpO₂) monitoring

The MAX30102 and MPU6050 share the same I2C bus.

```text
                    ESP32
                      │
              ┌───────┴───────┐
              │               │
           GPIO 21         GPIO 22
             SDA             SCL
              │               │
        ┌─────┴─────┐   ┌─────┴─────┐
        │  MPU6050  │   │  MAX30102 │
        └───────────┘   └───────────┘
```

---

# 5. ESP32 – MQ-3 Alcohol Sensor Connection

| MQ-3 | ESP32         |
| ---- | ------------- |
| VCC  | 5V/VIN*       |
| GND  | GND           |
| AO   | GPIO 34       |
| DO   | Optional GPIO |

### Purpose

The MQ-3 is used to detect alcohol presence in the rider's breath.

```text
MQ-3
 │
 ├── VCC ───► ESP32 VIN/5V*
 ├── GND ───► ESP32 GND
 └── AO  ───► ESP32 GPIO 34
```

**Important:** ESP32 GPIO pins are not 5V tolerant. If the MQ-3 analog output can reach 5V, use a voltage divider before connecting AO to GPIO 34.

