# 6. ESP32 – GPS Connection

The GPS module communicates with the ESP32 through UART.

| GPS | ESP32               |
| --- | ------------------- |
| VCC | Module-rated supply |
| GND | GND                 |
| TX  | GPIO 16 (RX)        |
| RX  | GPIO 17 (TX)        |

### Connection

```text
GPS TX ───────► ESP32 GPIO 16 (RX)
GPS RX ◄────── ESP32 GPIO 17 (TX)
GPS GND ──────► ESP32 GND
GPS VCC ──────► Module-rated supply
```

### Purpose

GPS provides:

* Real-time location
* Accident location
* Emergency location sharing
* Navigation support

---

# 7. ESP32 – Buzzer Connection

| Buzzer       | ESP32   |
| ------------ | ------- |
| Positive (+) | GPIO 33 |
| Negative (-) | GND     |

### Connection

```text
ESP32 GPIO 33
      │
      ▼
    Buzzer
      │
      ▼
     GND
```

The buzzer can provide an audible warning during:

* Drowsiness
* Alcohol detection
* Accident detection
* Emergency conditions

For higher-current buzzers, a transistor driver should be used instead of connecting the buzzer directly to the GPIO.

